weaknesses:
- id: W001_TEST_PASS_DESPITE_MISMATCHES
  severity: critical
  category: test_infrastructure
  title: Tests report PASS despite scoreboard mismatches
  affected_tests:
  - TestPowerOfTwoDataPattern
  - TestRandomized
  evidence:
  - 'TestPowerOfTwoDataPattern: status=pass, scoreboard_mismatches=62'
  - 'TestRandomized: status=pass, scoreboard_mismatches=76'
  - simulation_result.json shows all 10 tests with category=pass despite mismatches
  likely_cause: Test base class (HammingEncoderBaseTest) does not check scoreboard
    error count in report_phase or end_of_simulation_phase. Scoreboard only logs errors
    but doesn't raise UVM_FATAL or cause test failure.
  investigation_targets:
  - tb/test_classes.py (HammingEncoderBaseTest.run_phase)
  - tb/scoreboard.py (report_phase method)
  recommended_action: Add scoreboard error check in test's report_phase or end_of_simulation_phase
    that calls self.fail() or raises UVM_FATAL when scoreboard.errors > 0. Alternatively,
    have scoreboard report_phase raise uvm_fatal on errors.
  confidence: high
- id: W002_ASSERTIONS_ONLY_CHECK_PARITY_CONSISTENCY
  severity: high
  category: assertion_coverage
  title: Assertions verify parity equations hold but not functional correctness
  affected_tests:
  - TestAllZerosInput
  - TestAllOnesInput
  - TestAlternating1010
  - TestAlternating0101
  - TestSingleBitSetLSB
  - TestSingleBitSetMSB
  - TestMaximumInputValue
  - TestMinimumInputValue
  - TestPowerOfTwoDataPattern
  - TestRandomized
  evidence:
  - 'All 10 tests show assertion_failures: 0'
  - verification_plan.yaml documents 4 RTL discrepancies (wrong data-to-position mapping,
    wrong parity masks, wrong codeword bit mapping, wrong overall parity)
  - Assertions in assertions.py only check that parity equations evaluate to even
    (self-consistency), not that codeword matches input data per spec
  likely_cause: Assertion checkers (overall_parity_check, hamming_parity_p*_check)
    only verify the output codeword has even parity per Hamming equations. They do
    not verify data bits are placed in correct non-parity positions, or that parity
    bits correspond to the actual input data. A buggy codeword with internally consistent
    but functionally wrong parity passes these assertions.
  investigation_targets:
  - tb/assertions.py (all hamming_parity_*_check functions)
  - tb/env.py (start_phase where checkers are started)
  recommended_action: Add assertions that verify data bits appear in correct non-parity
    Hamming positions (e.g., check codeword[3] == data_in[0], codeword[5] == data_in[1],
    etc.). Add cross-check between input data and specific codeword bit positions
    per specification.
  confidence: high
- id: W003_DIRECTED_TESTS_DO_NOT_EXPOSE_KNOWN_BUGS
  severity: high
  category: test_coverage
  title: Directed tests use patterns that do not expose documented RTL bugs
  affected_tests:
  - TestAllZerosInput
  - TestAllOnesInput
  - TestAlternating1010
  - TestAlternating0101
  - TestSingleBitSetLSB
  - TestSingleBitSetMSB
  - TestMaximumInputValue
  - TestMinimumInputValue
  evidence:
  - 8 directed/corner-case tests show scoreboard_mismatches=0
  - TestPowerOfTwoDataPattern (walking 1s across 64 bits) shows 62 mismatches
  - TestRandomized (100 random values) shows 76 mismatches
  - verification_plan.yaml discrepancies DISCREPANCY_001 through DISCREPANCY_004 describe
    RTL bugs
  likely_cause: Directed test patterns (all zeros, all ones, alternating, single bit
    at LSB/MSB) happen to not trigger the specific RTL bugs (skipped position 3, wrong
    parity masks, bit 10 mapping error, overall parity inversion). Bugs are only exposed
    when data bits exercise the affected positions (position 3, parity mask differences,
    bit 10, bit 71).
  investigation_targets:
  - tb/sequences.py (SeqAllZerosInput, SeqAllOnesInput, SeqAlternating1010, SeqAlternating0101,
    SeqSingleBitSetLSB, SeqSingleBitSetMSB)
  - tb/test_classes.py (corresponding test classes)
  recommended_action: 'Add directed tests targeting each known bug: (1) data_in with
    bit 0 set (maps to Hamming position 3), (2) patterns that differentiate parity
    mask errors, (3) pattern exercising Hamming position 10/11, (4) pattern exercising
    Hamming position 71 for overall parity. Use reference model to compute expected
    values for these targeted patterns.'
  confidence: high
- id: W004_SCOREBOARD_DOES_NOT_INDEPENDENTLY_VERIFY_PARITY_INVARIANTS
  severity: medium
  category: scoreboard_completeness
  title: Scoreboard only compares against reference model, lacks independent parity
    invariant checks
  affected_tests:
  - TestAllZerosInput
  - TestAllOnesInput
  - TestAlternating1010
  - TestAlternating0101
  - TestSingleBitSetLSB
  - TestSingleBitSetMSB
  - TestMaximumInputValue
  - TestMinimumInputValue
  - TestPowerOfTwoDataPattern
  - TestRandomized
  evidence:
  - scoreboard.py only computes expected_codeword = encode(data_in) and compares with
    actual
  - No independent verification of Hamming parity checks or overall parity on actual
    DUT output
  - If reference model had same bug as RTL, scoreboard would not detect it
  likely_cause: Scoreboard relies solely on reference model comparison. No defensive
    check that actual DUT output satisfies SECDED parity invariants regardless of
    reference model.
  investigation_targets:
  - tb/scoreboard.py (run_phase comparison logic)
  recommended_action: 'Add independent parity invariant checks in scoreboard.run_phase:
    verify actual_codeword has even overall parity, and each Hamming parity check
    evaluates to 0. Log separate error if invariants violated even if reference model
    matches (would indicate common-mode bug).'
  confidence: medium
